One source file is a re-implementation, in TypeScript, of a routine of Pillow,
and says so at the top:

  * browser/src/resize.ts (from src/libImaging/Resample.c, the 8-bit path of
    ImagingResample with the bilinear filter, as of Pillow 10): rewritten for
    one layout (RGBA in, RGB out) and a resize of the whole image, so that a
    browser feeds the detector the same pixels that
    Image.resize(size, Image.BILINEAR) gives the Python package. The tests
    compare its output, byte for byte, with Pillow's.

Pillow is not bundled. The Python package uses it as an installed dependency.

